   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 465 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law relating\nto authorizing the city of Hudson to impose hotel and motel taxes, in relation\nto extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8345",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8345-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 465 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8345\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 465 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law\nrelating to authorizing the city of Hudson to impose hotel and motel\ntaxes, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would extend authorization for the City of Hudson to collect\nan occupancy tax on short-term lodgers.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 extends Chapter 465 of the Laws of 2016, which authorizes the\nCity of Hudson to impose an occupancy tax for hotels and motels, until\n2027.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe City of Hudson requested this legislation to extend the authori-\nzation for their hotel and motel tax. This authorization is set to\nexpire at the end of 2025, and this bill would extend it through 2027.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThis will generate revenue for the City of Hudson.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
